# Fingerprints gitleaks should not report. Currently none.
#
# Policy, if an entry is ever needed: pin the full fingerprint — commit, file,
# rule and line — so it can only ever silence the one occurrence named. Never
# add a rule-wide or path-wide exclusion; that turns a security gate into
# decoration, and nobody notices until it matters.
#
# A finding is a reason to fix the code first. The last entry here existed only
# because a superseded commit still sat in an unmerged branch's history, and it
# was removed the moment that branch was squash-merged.
